12) Security Notes
------------------------------------------------------------
Current state:
- Admin auth supports password_hash and legacy MD5.
- Admin login now regenerates session id on success to reduce session fixation risk.
- Admin API now enforces POST-only for state-changing actions, reducing CSRF surface on GET endpoints.
- Admin session cookies are hardened with strict mode, HttpOnly, and SameSite=Strict (Secure on HTTPS).
- Center incharge auth supports password_hash and legacy MD5 fallback.
- Candidate APIs include basic security headers (nosniff, frame, referrer policy).
- Candidate side disables common browser shortcuts/context menu and blocks refresh keys during active test.

Recommended future improvements:
- Migrate all remaining admin passwords to password_hash only.
- Add server-side rate limiting for login.
- Add explicit CSRF token validation for admin and center mutation requests (defense in depth).
- Replace wildcard CORS with restricted origin policy if needed.
- Add prepared statements for all dynamic SQL queries.

